Notebook[
 {
  Cell[
   "Lepton-quark scattering, step 2 (Tracer route): spin and colour algebra", 
   "Title"], Cell["Same task and same output format as the FeynCalc route, \
now with the classic Tracer package for the Dirac algebra.  Input: the \
amplitude records of step 1 (Results/Amplitudes.wl).  Output: \
Results/Tracer/Algebra.wl.  Run this file in a fresh kernel: Tracer and \
FeynCalc cannot be loaded together.\n\nHow a squared amplitude becomes a \
Tracer trace.  Every term of an amplitude is a coefficient times one open \
spinor chain per fermion line, ubar(pOut) W u(pIn), where W is a string of \
gamma matrices.  Summing over the spins of the outgoing fermion and inserting \
the density matrix of the incoming one gives, for the interference of term i \
with term j,\n\n   Tr[ pOut-slash W_i rho(pIn) Wbar_j ],   rho = pIn-slash/2 \
(spin average) or pIn-slash gamma5/2 (helicity difference),\n\nwith Wbar_j \
the reversed string of the conjugate term.  In Tracer this trace is G[line, \
pOut, W_i..., pIn, (G5,) Wbar_j...] once Spur[line] has been declared.  The \
coefficients are multiplied by the complex conjugate of the other \
coefficient; gluon polarizations are summed with -g^{mu nu}; the colour sums \
are the few SU(N) identities written below.\n\nTracer vocabulary (see \
Tracer.pdf, the manual distributed with the package): G[line, p, {mu}, ...] \
is the string p-slash gamma^mu ... on the given fermion line, traced when \
Spur[line] has been set; S[p,q] = p.q, S[p,{mu}] = p^mu, S[{mu},{nu}] = g^{mu \
nu}, and repeated indices in a product are contracted automatically; H[p,q] \
is the (D-4)-dimensional part of p.q; Eps is the four-dimensional epsilon \
tensor; VectorDimension[D] sets the dimension and AntiCommute[off] selects \
the HVBM gamma5, defined as gamma5 = (i/4!) eps_{mu nu rho sigma} gamma^mu \
gamma^nu gamma^rho gamma^sigma so that Tr[gamma5 gamma^a gamma^b gamma^c \
gamma^d] = +4 i Eps[a,b,c,d]; this is minus the FeynCalc convention used in \
the other routes, which is why the circular-photon density below carries the \
opposite sign.  Conventions as in the FeynCalc route: s = 2 l.k, t = -2 k.p, \
u = -2 l.p, D = 4 - 2 eps; real emission adds a = (k-r)^2, b = (p+r)^2, s4 = \
(lp+r)^2, and spe3 = rhat.rhat.", "Text"], Cell["Load", "Section"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \
\"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["LoadTracer[]", "Input"], 
  Cell["records = \
LoadAmplitudes[][\"Records\"];\nVectorDimension[D];\nAntiCommute[off];\nSpur[\
1]; Spur[2];\nShowRecords[Flatten[records[\"Born\"]]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["From records to traces", "Section"], Cell["conjugate[record] forms \
the complex conjugate: i -> -i, reversed gamma strings, transposed colour \
generators, conjugated polarization vectors, and fresh names for the Lorentz \
indices so that they are not confused with those of the amplitude.  \
sewTrace[line, chainL, chainR, spin] builds the Tracer string of one fermion \
line.  The spinors of the records tell which momentum is incoming (Uspinor) \
and outgoing (Ubar).", "Text"], Cell["conjugate[record_] := Module[{indices, \
fresh},\n  indices = Union[Cases[record, i_Symbol /; \
StringStartsQ[SymbolName[i], \"Lor\"] :> i, Infinity]];   (* every Lorentz \
index Lor1, Lor2, ... *)\n  fresh = Thread[indices -> (Symbol[\"c\" <> \
SymbolName[#]] & /@ indices)];\n  <|\"Coefficient\" -> \
(record[\"Coefficient\"] /. fresh /. {Complex[x_, y_] :> Complex[x, -y],\n    \
  ColorT[a_, i_, j_] :> ColorT[Reverse[a], j, i], PolVector[p_, i_, sign_] :> \
PolVector[p, i, -sign]}),\n    \"Chains\" -> (Reverse /@ record[\"Chains\"] \
/. fresh)|>];\n\noutgoing[chain_Chain] := First[Cases[chain, Ubar[p_] :> \
p]];\nincoming[chain_Chain] := First[Cases[chain, Uspinor[p_] :> \
p]];\nsewTrace[line_, chainL_, chainR_, spin_] := Inactive[G] @@ Join[{line, \
outgoing[chainL]}, TracerString[chainL],\n  {incoming[chainL]}, If[spin === \
\"Polarized\", {G5}, {}], TracerString[chainR]];   (* chainR is already \
reversed *)\n\nconjugate[records[\"Born\"][[1, 1]]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Colour.  The quark line carries either delta_{ij} (Born) or a \
generator (T^a)_{ij}.  Summed over external colours and averaged with 1/Nc: \
(T^a T^a)_{ij} = CF delta_{ij}, delta_{ii} = Nc, so that T^a_{ij} T^a_{ji} = \
CF Nc and delta_{ij} delta_{ij} = Nc.  Everything else in a coefficient is a \
scalar that Tracer understands: Den[q] = 1/q^2 -> 1/S[q,q], Metric -> \
S[{mu},{nu}]; polarization vectors are left for the explicit sums below.", 
   "Text"], Cell["colourSum = {ColorDelta[i_, i_] :> Nc, ColorDelta[i_, j_] \
/; !OrderedQ[{i, j}] :> ColorDelta[j, i],\n  ColorT[{a_}, i_, x_] \
ColorT[{a_}, x_, j_] :> CF ColorDelta[i, j],\n  ColorDelta[i_, j_]^2 :> Nc, \
ColorDelta[i_, j_] ColorDelta[j_, i_] :> Nc};\nscalars = {Den[q_] :> 1/S[q, \
q], Metric[i_, j_] :> S[{i}, {j}]};\ngluonSum = PolVector[r, i_, -1] \
PolVector[r, j_, 1] :> -S[{i}, {j}];\n\n(* interference of amplitude term i \
with conjugate term j, for the given spin choice *)\ninterference[termL_, \
termR_, spin_] := Module[{conj = conjugate[termR], coefficient, traces},\n  \
coefficient = termL[\"Coefficient\"] conj[\"Coefficient\"] //. colourSum /. \
gluonSum /. scalars;\n  traces = Times @@ MapThread[sewTrace[#1, #2, #3, \
spin] &, {Range[Length[termL[\"Chains\"]]], termL[\"Chains\"], \
conj[\"Chains\"]}];\n  coefficient traces];\n\n(* square of a list of \
amplitudes (lists of records), averaged over the two incoming spins (1/4) and \
the quark colour (1/Nc) *)\nsquare[amplitudes_, spin_] := Module[{terms = \
Flatten[amplitudes]},\n  Sum[interference[terms[[i]], terms[[j]], spin], {i, \
Length[terms]}, {j, Length[terms]}]/(4 Nc)];", "Input"], 
  Cell["Born: l q -> l q", "Section"], Cell["All Born momenta are \
four-dimensional: their hatted components H vanish.  Activate evaluates the \
traces; Tracer contracts the Lorentz indices shared by the two traces when \
the product is expanded.  The kinematics (OnShell) and the hatted components \
are declared inside Internal`InheritedBlock, which keeps them local to one \
process while retaining Tracer's own definitions of S and H.  The trace is \
shown before it is evaluated.", "Text"], Cell["fourDimensional[momenta_List] \
:= (Unprotect[H]; Scan[(H[#] = 0; H[#, _] = 0) &, momenta]; \
Protect[H]);\nbornTrace = square[records[\"Born\"], \"Polarized\"]", 
   "Input"], Cell["born = Association @ Table[spin -> \
Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H},\n  fourDimensional[{l, k, lp, p}];\n  \
OnShell[on, {l, 0}, {k, 0}, {lp, 0}, {p, 0}, {l, k, s/2}, {lp, p, s/2}, {l, \
lp, -t/2}, {k, p, -t/2}, {l, p, -u/2}, {k, lp, -u/2}];\n  \
Factor[Expand[Activate[square[records[\"Born\"], spin]]]]], {spin, \
{\"Unpolarized\", \"Polarized\"}}]", "Input"], Cell["Require[Simplify[(born[\
\"Unpolarized\"] - 2 ee^4 eq^2 ((s^2 + u^2)/t^2 - (4 - D)/2)) /. u -> -s - t] \
=== 0, \"Born square differs from the textbook \
result\"];\nRequire[Simplify[(born[\"Polarized\"] - 2 ee^4 eq^2 (s^2 - \
u^2)/t^2) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \"Polarized Born square differs from the \
expected result\"];", "Input"], Cell["Real emission: l q -> l q g", 
   "Section"], Cell["Now l, k, p are four-dimensional while the unobserved lp \
and r have hatted components, H[r,r] = H[lp,lp] = -H[lp,r] = spe3.  The two \
amplitude terms give a 2 x 2 matrix of interferences; the gluon sum -g^{mu \
nu} and the colour factor CF are included by interference[].", "Text"], 
  Cell["real = Association @ Table[spin -> Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H},\n  \
fourDimensional[{l, k, p}];\n  Unprotect[H]; H[r, r] = spe3; H[lp, lp] = \
spe3; H[lp, r] = -spe3; Protect[H];\n  OnShell[on, {l, 0}, {k, 0}, {lp, 0}, \
{p, 0}, {r, 0}, {l, k, s/2}, {k, p, -t/2}, {l, p, -u/2}, {k, r, -a/2}, {p, r, \
b/2},\n    {l, lp, -(a + b + t)/2}, {l, r, (s + t + u + a + b)/2}, {k, lp, (s \
+ t + a)/2}, {lp, p, -(t + u + b)/2}, {lp, r, (s + t + u)/2}];\n  \
Factor[Expand[Activate[square[records[\"Real\"], spin]]]]], {spin, \
{\"Unpolarized\", \"Polarized\"}}];\nFactor[real[\"Polarized\"] /. spe3 -> \
0]", "Input"], Cell["Photon-quark Born: gamma q -> q g", "Section"], 
  Cell["Here only one fermion line exists.  The unpolarized photon is \
averaged with -g^{mu nu}/(D-2) and the quark spin with 1/2; square[] supplies \
1/4, so the unpolarized result is multiplied by 2/(D-2).  For the helicity \
difference the photon density is -i eps^{mu nu q k}/(2 q.k) (Tracer's Eps is \
minus FeynCalc's with $LeviCivitaSign = -1) and the quark density k-slash \
gamma5/2: the factor 1/4 of square[] is replaced by 1/2.", "Text"], 
  Cell["photonSums = {PolVector[q, i_, 1] PolVector[q, j_, -1] :> -S[{i}, \
{j}], PolVector[r, i_, -1] PolVector[r, j_, 1] :> -S[{i}, \
{j}]};\ncircularPhoton = {PolVector[q, i_, 1] PolVector[q, j_, -1] :> -I \
Eps[{i}, {j}, q, k]/(2 S[q, k]), PolVector[r, i_, -1] PolVector[r, j_, 1] :> \
-S[{i}, {j}]};\nphoton = Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H},\n  \
fourDimensional[{q, k, p, r}];\n  OnShell[on, {q, 0}, {k, 0}, {p, 0}, {r, 0}, \
{q, k, sh/2}, {k, p, -th/2}, {q, p, -uh/2}, {p, r, sh/2}, {k, r, -uh/2}, {q, \
r, -th/2}];\n  <|\"Unpolarized\" -> Factor[Expand[Activate[2/(D - 2) \
square[records[\"Photon\"], \"Unpolarized\"] /. photonSums]]],\n    \
\"Polarized\" -> Factor[Expand[Activate[2 square[records[\"Photon\"], \
\"Polarized\"] /. circularPhoton]]]|>]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Virtual: the one-loop vertex", "Section"], 
  Cell["The vertex graph has the quark chain ubar(p) gamma^a (p-slash - \
loop-slash) gamma^mu (k-slash - loop-slash) gamma_a u(k) (indices named Lor3, \
Lor4 are contracted by the gluon propagator's metric).  After loop \
integration this current is a form factor times the Born current gamma^mu, so \
the ratio\n\n   Tr[p-slash W_vertex k-slash gamma_mu] / Tr[p-slash gamma^mu \
k-slash gamma_mu]\n\nis the scalar integrand of the form factor.  Written in \
the inverse propagators d0 = loop^2, d1 = (loop-k)^2, d2 = (loop-p)^2 (2 \
loop.k = d0 - d1, 2 loop.p = d0 - d2), each monomial lowers the power of a \
propagator: the result is a combination of VirtualIntegral[n0,n1,n2] = \
integral of 1/(d0^n0 d1^n1 d2^n2), the same family as in the FeynCalc route.  \
The coefficient of the vertex record relative to the Born record gives the \
normalization: gs^2 CF times the three propagators (and the factor that \
converts FeynArts' loop measure, fixed in step 3).", "Text"], 
  Cell["vertex = records[\"VirtualVertex\"][[1, 1]];\nbornRecord = \
records[\"Born\"][[1, 1]];\nquarkChain = First[Select[vertex[\"Chains\"], \
outgoing[#] === p &]];\nquarkChain", "Input"], 
  Cell["word = TracerString[quarkChain] /. Metric -> Sequence;\ngluonIndices \
= Cases[vertex[\"Coefficient\"], Metric[i_, j_] /; FreeQ[{i, j}, Lor1 | Lor2] \
:> {i, j}][[1]];\nword = word /. {gluonIndices[[2]]} -> {gluonIndices[[1]]};  \
       (* contract the gluon propagator metric *)\ncurrentIndex = \
First[Complement[Cases[word, {i_} :> i], gluonIndices]];\nprojector = \
Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H},\n  OnShell[on, {k, 0}, {p, 0}, {k, p, \
-t/2}];\n  Factor[(G @@ Join[{1, p}, word, {k, {currentIndex}}])/G[1, p, \
{currentIndex}, k, {currentIndex}]]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["numerator = Expand[projector /. {S[loop, loop] -> d0, S[loop, k] -> \
(d0 - d1)/2, S[loop, p] -> (d0 - d2)/2}];\nvirtualFamily = Total[(#[[2]] \
VirtualIntegral @@ ({1, 1, 1} - #[[1]])) & /@ CoefficientRules[numerator, \
{d0, d1, d2}]]", "Input"], Cell["Normalization relative to the FeynCalc \
route.  There the family multiplied 2 CF Pi^2 gs^2 after dividing the \
interference 2 Re(M1 M0 by |M0|^2.  Here the ratio of the two records' \
coefficients is CF gs^2 (with the colour sum) times the loop propagators and \
a factor -I from FeynArts' loop measure; the convention of step 3, which \
inserts the master integral with measure d^D loop/(i Pi^(D/2)), is fixed by \
comparing the virtual double pole with the real one.  We keep the same family \
normalization as the FeynCalc route so that step 3 is route independent.", 
   "Text"], Cell["relativeCoefficient = \
Simplify[(vertex[\"Coefficient\"]/bornRecord[\"Coefficient\"]) //. colourSum \
/.\n  {Den[loop] -> 1, Den[k - loop] -> 1, Den[p - loop] -> 1, Den[loop - k] \
-> 1, Den[loop - p] -> 1, Metric[gluonIndices[[1]], gluonIndices[[2]]] -> \
1}];\nRequire[Simplify[relativeCoefficient - (-I) CF gs^2] === 0, \
\"Unexpected vertex coefficient\", relativeCoefficient];\nvirtualFamily", 
   "Input"], Cell["Save", "Section"], Cell["algebra = <|\"Born\" -> born, \
\"Real\" -> real, \"Photon\" -> photon, \"VirtualFamily\" -> \
virtualFamily|>;\nSaveResult[\"Algebra\", algebra, \
\"Tracer\"];\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
